+++ b/docs/development.md
@@ -56,6 +56,17 @@ bin/rails dev:email
 
 Under the hood, this will create or remove `tmp/email-dev.txt`.
 
+### Push notifications
+
+Web push needs a VAPID key pair, which Fizzy reads from the `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` environment variables. Generate one with `bin/rails push:vapid_keys`, export the two variables, and start the server:
+
+```sh
+eval "$(bin/rails push:vapid_keys | sed 's/^/export /')"
+bin/dev
+```
+
+Then turn on push notifications for your browser from the notification settings. Browsers treat `app.fizzy.localhost` as a secure context, so Chrome and Firefox will subscribe and deliver pushes there. Safari only pushes to installed web apps, which need `https`: `bin/dev --tailscale` gives you a URL for that.
+
 ## SaaS gem
 
 37signals bundles Fizzy with [`fizzy-saas`](https://github.com/basecamp/fizzy/tree/main/saas), a companion gem that links Fizzy with our billing system and contains our production setup.
